\lispPackageChapter{livermore/statistics}

The \texttt{livermore/statistics} package is a small set of sample statistics
on sequences.  Each generic takes \texttt{\&key key start end}.  The
underlying sequence helpers come from $\Sigma$~\cite{gore-sigma}.

\section{Generics}

\lispGenericSubsection{arithmetic-mean}

The sample mean $\bar{x}$.  Returns \texttt{nil} on an empty sequence.

\lispGenericSubsection{sample-variance}

The second central moment $s_N^2$, divided by $N$.

\lispGenericSubsection{unbiased-sample-variance}

The unbiased estimator $s_{N-1}^2$, divided by $N-1$.  Returns
\texttt{nil} when the sequence has fewer than two elements.

\lispGenericSubsection{sample-standard-deviation}

$\sqrt{s_N^2}$.

\lispGenericSubsection{unbiased-sample-standard-deviation}

$\sqrt{s_{N-1}^2}$.

\lispGenericSubsection{stat-report}

Prints the mean, unbiased standard deviation, minimum, and maximum of
\lispVar{data} to \lispVar{destination}.

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(stat-report \lispVar{destination} \lispVar{data} \&key key start end pre-string format-string post-string)}

\lispExamples

\begin{lstlisting}
(arithmetic-mean '(1 2 3))           ; => 2
(unbiased-sample-variance '(1 2 3))  ; => 1
\end{lstlisting}
